sequenceDiagram
    participant Browser as Browser / approver UI
    participant Api as ASP.NET Core pipeline
    participant Middleware as SessionAuthMiddleware
    participant Store as SessionStore
    participant Filter as RequireRoleAttribute
    participant Controller as ApprovalsController
    participant Handle as ApiControllerBase.Handle
    participant Service as ApprovalService
    participant RepoContract as IInvoiceRepository
    participant RepoImpl as InMemoryInvoiceRepository
    participant Response as HTTP response

    Note over Browser,Response: Verified source files: Program.cs, SessionAuthMiddleware.cs, RequireRoleAttribute.cs, ApprovalsController.cs, ApiControllerBase.cs, ApprovalService.cs, InMemoryInvoiceRepository.cs

    Browser->>Api: POST /api/approvals/{invoiceId}/approve
    Api->>Middleware: request enters middleware
    Middleware->>Store: Get(token)
    Store-->>Middleware: UserSession(username, role) or null
    alt Missing or invalid bearer token
        Middleware-->>Response: HTTP 401 Unauthorized
        Note right of Middleware: SessionAuthMiddleware.InvokeAsync checks token and returns StatusCodes.Status401Unauthorized when session is null.
    else Token is valid
        Middleware-->>Api: continue
        Api->>Filter: OnActionExecuting
        Filter->>Filter: session = HttpContext.Items["session"] as UserSession
        alt Session missing or role not allowed
            Filter-->>Response: HTTP 403 Forbidden
            Note right of Filter: RequireRoleAttribute.OnActionExecuting sets StatusCodeResult(StatusCodes.Status403Forbidden) when session is null or role is not in the allowed set.
        else Role allowed
            Filter-->>Api: continue
            Api->>Controller: ApprovalsController.Approve(invoiceId)
            Controller->>Handle: Handle(() => _approvals.Approve(invoiceId, HttpContext.GetSession().Username))
            Handle->>Service: _approvals.Approve(invoiceId, session.Username)
            Service->>RepoContract: GetById(invoiceId)
            RepoContract->>RepoImpl: InMemoryInvoiceRepository.GetById(id)
            RepoImpl-->>Service: Invoice
            Service->>Service: EnsurePending(invoice)
            Service->>Service: set Status = Approved
            Service->>Service: set DecidedBy = approver
            Service->>Service: set DecidedAt = DateTime.UtcNow
            Service->>RepoContract: Update(invoice)
            RepoContract->>RepoImpl: InMemoryInvoiceRepository.Update(invoice)
            RepoImpl-->>Service: void
            alt Invoice not found
                Service-->>Handle: throws KeyNotFoundException
                Handle-->>Controller: NotFound(new { error = ex.Message })
                Controller-->>Response: HTTP 404 Not Found
            else Invoice not pending
                Service-->>Handle: throws InvalidOperationException
                Handle-->>Controller: Conflict(new { error = ex.Message })
                Controller-->>Response: HTTP 409 Conflict
            else Approval succeeds
                Service-->>Handle: Invoice
                Handle-->>Controller: Ok(updated Invoice)
                Controller-->>Response: HTTP 200 OK + Invoice JSON
            end
        end
    end

    Note over Handle,Response: ApiControllerBase.Handle also catches ArgumentException and returns HTTP 400 Bad Request. This mapping is implemented in the base handler, even though the approve method itself does not throw ArgumentException in this path.
